../ml4t-data/dukascopy_rebuild/deu_jpn_index_trading_break_calendar.json:239:      "before_regular_breaks": "The provider minute-history metadata predates Dukascopy live CFD trading. Before regular CFD breaks became effective on 2015-04-20, canonical qualification preserves the explicit provider m1 grid only inside source-qualified weekly boundaries: Sunday reopen and Friday close shift with respective DST (EU DST for DEU, US DST for JPN), Saturday is closed. From the 2014-09-10 live-CFD launch through 2015-04-19, every Friday/Saturday/Sunday boundary day is source-probed. Out-of-session non-flat rows fail closed unless confirmed via uncached provider refetch; confirmed snapshots are preserved as quality anomalies without widening the nominal trading session.",
../ml4t-data/dukascopy_rebuild/deu_jpn_index_trading_break_calendar.json:240:      "day_session": "From 2015-04-20 through 2018-04-11, day-session completeness is qualified from Dukascopy notices plus m1 source evidence. DEU.IDX/EUR operates on 06:00-20:00 GMT (summer) / 07:00-21:00 GMT (winter) following European DST, shifting to 06:05-19:59 (summer) / 07:05-20:59 (winter) in August/September 2017. JPN.IDX/JPY starts on 06:00-20:00 in 2015 summer, then adopts 01:00-20:00 (US summer) / 01:00-21:00 (US winter) following US DST from November 2015, shifting to 01:05-19:59 (summer) / 01:05-20:59 (winter) in August/September 2017. Weekends are closed.",
