run_log/fx_support_ml4t_execution_20261008_v2/completion_report.md:13:Commission is 0.000025 of executed notional per side. Base slippage is 0.00005 per side. Stress slippage is 0.00010 per side. Net R divides native net trade PnL, including fees and executed-price slippage, by actual entry quantity times executed entry price less origin support. The stop-risk budget uses the support level; exit slippage, fees and price gaps can increase realized loss. Daily Sharpe uses native combined portfolio equity, UTC daily closes, all calendar days including flat and weekend days, and annualization of 365.25. Maximum drawdown uses the native continuous five-minute equity series. Prague day statistics use observed completed-bar equity and cannot establish exact FTMO midnight loss-limit compliance across gaps.
run_log/fx_support_ml4t_execution_20261008_v2/completion_report.md:21:The initial v2 P0 passed the timing and single-position fixtures. A later independent review found that default EXIT_FIRST allowed an intrabar EURUSD stop to release risk before a simultaneous GBPUSD opening entry. The corrected native PRIORITY order processes all opening entries before intrabar exits, then STOPs before LIMITs. The new two-pair fixture proves that a changed future intrabar low cannot change opening size, equity, risk or leverage. The native Engine continues to own fill matching, OCO cancellation, cash, commissions, slippage and trade PnL. No custom simulation or portfolio metric loop was used.
