ut/ournews/cfd-trading-launched-on-live-accounts/","claim":"Dukascopy announced live CFD trading on regular LIVE self-trading accounts on 2014-09-10."},"regular_breaks_introduced":{"published_date":"2015-04-17","effective_date":"2015-04-20","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/cfd-trading-schedule-changes/","claim":"Dukascopy announced regular trading breaks for all available CFDs effective 2015-04-20 because of low off-market liquidity."},"daylight_schedule_notices":[{"published_date":"2015-03-06","effective_date":"2015-03-08","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/change-to-daylight-saving-time-dbl200254/","claim":"Dukascopy announced the US daylight-saving transition effective 2015-03-08 and return to winter schedule on 2015-11-01."},{"published_date":"2016-03-09","effective_date":"2016-03-13","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/change-to-daylight-saving-time-dbl200533/","claim":"Dukascopy announced the US daylight-saving transition effective 2016-03-13 and return to winter schedule on 2016-11-06."},{"published_date":"2017-03-06","effective_date":"2017-03-12","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/change-to-daylight-saving-time-dbl200750/","claim":"Dukascopy announced the US daylight-saving transition effective 2017-03-12 and return to winter schedule on 2017-11-05."},{"published_date":"2017-10-26","effective_date":"2017-11-05","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/daylight-savings-time-ends-dbl200887/","claim":"Dukascopy announced the North American winter-time transition effective 2017-11-05."}],"extended_index_hours":{"published_date":"2018-04-12","effective_date":"2018-04-12","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/dukascopy-expands-trading-time-on-cfd-indices/","claim":"Dukascopy announced expanded trading time for US and EU CFD indices on 2018-04-12."},"modern_regular_hours":{"url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/cfd/range-of-markets/","claim":"USA500.IDX/USD and USATECH.IDX/USD use Sun-Fri 22:00-20:15 GMT with 20:15-22:00 breaks in US summer time, and Sun-Fri 23:00-21:15 GMT with 21:15-23:00 breaks in US winter time."},"archived_notice_anchors":[{"event":"US Independence Day 2015","date":"2015-07-03","declared_close":"16:45","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/us-independence-day-trading-hours"},{"event":"Presidents Day 2016","date":"2016-02-15","declared_close":"18:00","next_day":"2016-02-16","declared_reopen":"07:00","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/full-news/beware-of-reduced-liquidity-on-monday-15-february-due-to-us-market-closure-on-presidents-day-/"},{"event":"US Independence Day eve 2017","date":"2017-07-03","declared_close":"15:45","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/holiday-on-4-july-in-the-us/"},{"event":"Memorial Day 2018","date":"2018-05-28","declared_close":"17:00","declared_reopen":"22:00","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/memorial-day-holiday-monday-28-may"},{"event":"US Independence Day eve 2018","date":"2018-07-03","declared_close":"17:15","declared_reopen":"22:00","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/us-independence-day-on-wednesday-4th-july"},{"event":"US Independence Day 2018","date":"2018-07-04","declared_close":"17:00","declared_reopen":"22:00","url":"https://www.dukascopy.com/swiss/english/about/ournews/us-independence-day-on-wednesday-4th-july"}]},"interpretation":{"before_regular_breaks":"The provider minute-history metadata predates Dukascopy live CFD trading. Before regular CFD breaks became effective on 2015-04-20, canonical qualification preserves the explicit provider m1 grid only inside source-qualified US-index weekly boundaries: Sunday reopen and Friday close shift with US DST, Saturday is closed. From the 2014-09-10 live-CFD launch through 2015-04-19, every Friday/Saturday/Sunday boundary day is source-probed on both indices. Any non-flat row outside the nominal grid fails closed unless the same exact timestamp is present on both indices, matches the qualified pre-break Sunday snapshot pattern, and survives an uncached source refetch. Such rows are preserved as provider-quality anomalies and do not widen the trading-session interval. Flat/zero-volume rows inside the qualified grid are preserved and are not claimed to represent executable CFD liquidity.","day_session":"From 2015-04-20 through 2018-04-11, US-index day-session completeness is qualified from Dukascopy notices plus paired m1 source sentinels. It is not computed from a generic DST formula: 2015 delays the winter grid until 2015-11-06; 2016 switches on 2016-03-14 and 2016-11-07; 2017 has explicit 2017-03-13/14 transition days, uses the 06:00-20:00-candle grid from 2017-03-15, shifts the open to 06:05 on 2017-08-04, shifts the final source minute to 19:59 on 2017-09-05, then uses 07:05-20:59 from 2017-11-06; 2018 returns to 06:05-19:59 on 2018-03-12. Weekends are closed.","modern_session":"From 2018-04-12 onward, modern extended-hours semantics apply; 2018-04-12 is an explicit transition day because its UTC day began under the old schedule and reopened under the new schedule.","holiday_exceptions":"Holiday candidates are discovery inputs only. A source-derived shortened/closed session may truncate only the first scheduled trading segment of the UTC day, and only when a long flat provider interval common to both US index source series reaches that segment's scheduled end with a matching uncached refetch. Later scheduled reopen segments remain expected-open unless explicit Dukascopy schedule evidence says otherwise. Start-only inactivity after a scheduled reopen is retained as provider data and never reclassified as a delayed open. Representative archived Dukascopy notices anchor the interpretation."},"authority_manifest_identity":"10ed9c5d3da26979a89fabfbbc31c0ad6f5706591740fdb3fbbd077baa6ad536"},"candidate_generator":{"schema_ver