## Completed

I ran both frozen variants through the native `ml4t.backtest` engine on the full available history, from 2013-01-01 through 2026-07-14. The cost-aware run produced **5,150 closed trades**, **$207,805.90 net PnL**, **$40.35 average net PnL per trade**, **1.376 profit factor**, and **1.730 daily-equity Sharpe**. Modeled costs totaled $38,625.

I corrected the 30-minute bar alignment for the repeated fall DST hour and reran both variants. The corrected trade and fill values match the superseded run; timestamps in the final trade and fill ledgers are explicitly marked UTC. All trades held 30 minutes or less, the daily entry cap held, and there were no late boundary exits.

The source audit found **444,329 minutes missing from calendar-expected open intervals**, including a 22,411-minute timestamp gap. The engine also flagged 42 same-minute entry/stop ambiguities. These limits, the illustrative costs, and the unverified CFD-to-CME mapping mean this supports only a finding on the observed Dukascopy proxy. It does not validate CME NQ performance or approve trading.

